## 7. DO-D11 handback (changed the Compose sequence; not run)
109:1. **The Compose half is unverified.** The `create_host_path: false` mount, the refusal of an unset `MTH_BACKUP_ROOT`, the root `backup` service writing 0700/0600, and step 2 with `--user 0:0` were not run, because there is no Docker daemon. They run on the orchestrator's host (D-243 Q1), and backup-restore.md §10 says so. The scripts' behaviour is proven on a disposable PostgreSQL (T-E10 to 
110:2. **Step 2 of §3.2 now runs the app image as root (`--user 0:0`).** It is a pre-existing defect I fixed along the way. Before this change the `backup` service (root) created the set as root 0755, so the app image's user (uid 10001, `deploy/docker/Dockerfile` l.95) could not write `evidence/attachments.json` either. Running that one command as root is the least invasive fix. The alternative i

